            <h2>Train Duration, Distance, and Travel Time Overview</h2>
            <p>Traveling from Baltimore to Orlando covers roughly 791 miles (1,273 km) along the East Coast, linking the Mid-Atlantic with Central Florida. Although this isn’t a high‑speed rail corridor like in Europe, Amtrak's long-distance trains offer a steady and pleasant pace, often making the trip more enjoyable than a long drive.</p>

