            <h2>Tips to Save Money on This Route</h2>
            <p>Managing the cost of train travel from Baltimore to Orlando is easier with some planning and smart strategies. Prices can vary depending on timing, class, and travel season, but with the right approach, you can save money without compromising comfort.</p>
            <h3>Plan for Better Price Options</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Advance Booking:</b> Purchasing tickets days or weeks ahead often secures the lowest fares, especially for Coach seating.</li>
                <li><b>Compare Departures:</b>  Check multiple departure times to find the most economical option.</li>
                <li><b>Seating Choices: </b> Coach is generally cheaper than Business Class; consider if comfort trade-offs are acceptable.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Travel During Off-Peak Hours</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Midday Trains:</b> Often less crowded, with fares sometimes lower than peak season trains.</li>
                <li><b>Avoid Peak Travel:</b> Holidays, spring break, and summer often lead to higher prices and limited availability.</li>
                <li><b>Flexibility Helps: </b>Traveling on weekdays can reduce cost and provide a more relaxed environment.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Stay Flexible with Your Travel Plans</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Adjusting your departure by a few days or considering different travel weeks can unlock cheaper options.</li>
                <li>Flexibility may also improve seating availability, especially in Business Class and Sleeper cars.</li>
                <li>Being open to slightly longer travel times or non-prime hours can balance cost and convenience.</li>
            </ul>
