            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3>1. How long is the train from Baltimore to Orlando?</h3>
            <p>The train journey typically takes 19 to 22.5 hours, depending on the service and the number of stops.</p>

            <h3>2. What is the fastest train from Baltimore to Orlando?</h3>
            <p>The fastest option is Amtrak Silver Meteor or Floridian, which can complete the journey in approximately 18 hours and 57 minutes with direct service.</p>

            <h3>3. How much does a train ticket from Baltimore to Orlando cost?</h3>
            <p>Ticket prices generally fall between:</p>
            <p><b>$133-$200 for early booking on the coach</b></p>
            <p><b>$200-$310 for standard Coach fares</b></p>
            <p><b>$260-$400 for Business Class</b></p>
            <p><b>$400-$600+ for Sleeper accommodations or last-minute travel</b></p>

            <h3>4. Are there direct trains from Baltimore to Orlando?</h3>
            <p>Yes, Amtrak Silver Meteor and Floridian trains are direct, so there’s no need for transfers.</p>

            <h3>5. What amenities are available onboard?</h3>
            <p>Trains offer comfortable seating, Wi-Fi (where available), power outlets, a café car, dining car, and luggage space. Sleeper cars include private rooms and meals.</p>

            <h3>6. Is train travel faster than driving?</h3>
            <p>Depending on traffic, driving may take 13-15 hours, while the train is generally stress-free, predictable, and allows you to rest during the journey.</p>

            <h3>7. Can you travel from Baltimore to Orlando in one day?</h3>
            <p>The journey is an overnight trip, with departures typically arriving the following day.</p>

            <h3>8. Which station in Baltimore do trains depart from?</h3>
            <p>Most trains depart from Baltimore Penn Station, located in downtown Baltimore. Some airport connections exist but require extra planning.</p>

            <h3>9. Which station do trains arrive at in Orlando?</h3>
            <p>Trains arrive at Orlando Health/Amtrak Station, conveniently located just south of downtown and easily accessible by SunRail and local buses.</p>

            <h3>10. Is Business Class or Sleeper worth it?</h3>
            <p>Yes, Business Class offers extra legroom and a quieter environment. At the same time, Sleeper accommodations provide private rooms and include meals, making both ideal for travelers seeking more comfort during the 19+ hour journey.</p>













